        <h1>Neo Calendar</h1>
        <div class="post-meta"><time>Neo Calendar · Read-only Google Calendar integration</time></div>
      </div>
      <div class="post-content">

<p><strong>Neo Calendar</strong> is a Google Calendar application that provides read-only access to your calendar events.</p>

<h2>Purpose of this app</h2>

<p>The app reads your calendar to prepare a morning briefing: today's appointments, upcoming events, and family or shared calendar items — summarised in one place. It exists so you can see your day at a glance.</p>

<h2>What this app can and cannot do</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Reads</strong> calendar events (read-only).</li>
  <li><strong>Never</strong> creates, modifies, or deletes events.</li>
  <li><strong>Never</strong> shares your data with any third party.</li>
  <li>Runs on private home hardware, owned by the app's operator.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data access and consent</h2>

<p>Neo Calendar requests only the <code>calendar.readonly</code> scope. Access is granted through Google's standard OAuth consent screen and can be revoked at any time from your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google Account permissions page</a>. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for details.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>

<p>Questions about Neo Calendar? Contact the app owner.</p>

